# The OAuth authorization server's private signing JWKS: a complete P-256/ES256
# private key document (see README "Production OAuth"). Development and test
# generate a process-local ephemeral key, so this is only read when
# NODE_ENV=production — but there it is effectively required, not optional.
# Without it oidc-route.ts replaces every OAuth route with a 503
# `oauth_not_configured`, including /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource — the
# URL the MCP endpoint's 401 names in WWW-Authenticate. An MCP client then has
# no way to discover the authorization server and cannot authenticate at all
# (ADR 0007 D4). Leave unset for local development.
OAUTH_JWKS=

# Identity OAuth 2.1 provider — static "discourse" client for the forum's
# "Log in with Beancount" button. Its non-secret client metadata lives in
# src/features/oauth/data/config.ts; issuer and signing keys remain deployment
# inputs in src/config/config.ts. This is the ONLY client-specific env var the
# feature reads. A real secret is required
# (not public/PKCE-only) — discourse-openid-connect always sends client
# authentication, and oidc-provider rejects an empty secret rather than
# treating it as "none". Leave unset to keep the client disabled — the server
# boots normally either way (buildStaticOAuthClients() registers no client).
# Unrelated to the DISCOURSE_SSO_* vars above (DiscourseConnect, not OAuth2).
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
OAUTH_DISCOURSE_CLIENT_SECRET=TODO

